# Chatwoot Core

## Approach

- MVP focus: least code change, happy-path only
- Ship the happy path first; add guards only when production proves they need them
- Prefer minimal, readable code over clever abstractions — extract when a pattern repeats, not preemptively
- Break complex tasks into small, testable units; iterate after confirmation
- Avoid writing specs unless explicitly asked
- Pick one approach — no duplicate versions of the same logic

## Structure & naming

- One responsibility per file — split large controllers, services, or components before they become hard to scan
- Use descriptive domain names: `ConversationFinder`, `Messages::AudioTranscriptionService`
- PascalCase components, camelCase events, Ruby snake_case
- Replace business-significant literals with named constants

## Comments, cleanup & docs

- Comments explain non-obvious intent or trade-offs — write in English
- Remove dead code, commented-out code, empty `rescue`/`catch` blocks, unused exports
- Never generate standalone docs (README, changelogs, wiki) unless explicitly requested

## Errors

- Handle failures explicitly — use `lib/custom_exceptions/`; do not swallow errors

## Commits

- Conventional Commits: `type(scope): subject` — e.g. `feat(auth): add user authentication`
- Do not reference Claude in commit messages

## Translations

- Only update English — other languages are community-maintained
- Backend → `config/locales/en.yml`
- Dashboard → `app/javascript/dashboard/i18n/locale/en/*.json`
- Widget / survey → `app/javascript/{widget,survey}/i18n/locale/en.json`

## Frontend & branding

- Message bubbles: use `components-next/` (legacy bubbles are deprecated)
- Vue/JS conventions and Tailwind styling → `vue-frontend.mdc`
- User-facing "Chatwoot" strings → `replaceInstallationName` from `shared/composables/useBranding`
